.TITLE "touch"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Updates the access and modification times of files on macOS. If a specified file
does not exist, `touch` creates an empty new file. This command is commonly
used to create empty files, or to simply update timestamps without modifying
file content.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**createfile**

.DIV "TLDR"
**touch __file.txt__**
Creates a new empty __file.txt__ if it does not exist, or updates its timestamps if it does.
> __file.txt__: The path to the file to create or update.

**touch __file1.txt__ __file2.txt__**
Creates or updates multiple files (__file1.txt__, __file2.txt__) simultaneously.
> __file1.txt__: The path to the first file. | __file2.txt__: The path to the second file.

**touch -a __file.txt__**
Updates only the access time of __file.txt__.
> __-a__: access time only flag | __file.txt__: The path to the file.

**touch -m __file.txt__**
Updates only the modification time of __file.txt__.
> __-m__: modification time only flag | __file.txt__: The path to the file.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`touch` is a simple yet effective command for file management. It is often
used in scripting to trigger build processes that rely on file modification
times, or to quickly create placeholder files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ls** **mac:mkdir**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/touch.html
